WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.799
Sabrina Spellman is back to raise hell in
Greendale and uncover the secret truth about

00:00:05.799 --> 00:00:07.959
herself in Part 2 of her Chilling Adventures.

00:00:07.959 --> 00:00:12.490
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm explaining everything you need

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:16.180
to know about the second season of Chilling
Adventures of Sabrina, the hidden clues you

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.260
missed in the episode finale, and what to
look forward to in Season 3.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.410
Of course, there'll be spoilers, so take care
if you're not all caught up.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:27.970
The second season of Chilling Adventures finally
reveals Sabrina's true parentage.

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:32.730
As she goes to confront Lucifer who's risen
from Hell into Greendale, he reveals that

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:35.350
he, the Dark Lord, is Sabrina's father.

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:39.809
It's a Darth Vader-esque moment as Sabrina
learns her real feather is the big bad and

00:00:39.809 --> 00:00:43.809
she's not the half-witch, half-mortal she
always thought she was.

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:47.609
Sabrina's conception and birth are a twist
on the biblical story of Mary and Joseph where

00:00:47.609 --> 00:00:52.719
it was the Holy Spirit, not Joseph, who conceived
the baby Jesus in Mary.

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:56.440
Biblical references abound throughout this
season with the first episode starting with

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:00.729
a dream Sabrina has of her birth which is
reminiscent of traditional Christian nativity

00:01:00.729 --> 00:01:01.729
scenes.

00:01:01.729 --> 00:01:05.110
The episode is called The Epiphany with the
Three Kings of Hell, an obvious play on the

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:08.070
3 Wise Men or Kings who visit Jesus.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:12.780
As Ambrose explains in the finale, the Dark
Lord's plan "in siring a babe of a witch,

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.219
mortal, and infernal blood" is to pervert
the Holy Trinity.

00:01:16.219 --> 00:01:20.700
Before this revelation, incredible powers
that Sabrina never knew she had are gradually

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:21.700
unveiled.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:25.840
In the sixth episode during the witch-hunters'
attack, they place a crown of thorns on her

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:31.000
head and pierce her body three times with
crossbow arrows, evoking parallels with Christ's

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.470
crucifixion.

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:37.420
Sabrina dies but is resurrected, like Christ,
and then as she levitates with hands ablaze,

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:41.700
she sets the witch hunters on fire in a scene
that reminded me of the end of the first season

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:46.250
when Sabrina summoned hellfire against the
Greendale 13, becoming only the fourth witch

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.299
in history to ever achieve that.

00:01:48.299 --> 00:01:52.510
She is even able to resurrect Melvin and Elspeth
who the witch hunters had murdered.

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:53.780
"You're not a witch.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.140
What are you?"

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:59.840
"I am the Dark Lord's sword!"

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.869
From Sabrina's words, it's clear that these
amazing powers stem from her infernal blood

00:02:03.869 --> 00:02:05.829
or conception by the Dark Lord.

00:02:05.829 --> 00:02:10.060
Harvey also points out to Sabrina that she
resembles Jean Grey with her phoenix powers

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:14.200
in this scene:
"Jean Grey was this really powerful mutant.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.450
When she was on the verge of death something
saved her."

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:22.290
Like Sabrina, when Jean Grey had access to
the Phoenix Force, her power levels went insane

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:26.090
and there were even instances where the force
brought the dead back to life.

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:30.000
These miracles are explored in more detail
in the seventh episode with further parallels

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.780
being drawn between Sabrina and Jesus.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:36.870
Sabrina restores Roz's sight by getting her
to wash her eyes, in a miracle not dissimilar

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:42.040
to how Jesus gave sight to a blind man when
he ordered him to go wash in a pool of water.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:46.100
Sabrina's devilish DNA seems to give her powers
unavailable to her witch brethren.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:51.090
And initially, in her often impetuous way,
she assumes there's no downside to these almost

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:54.690
unlimited abilities, much to the consternation
of her aunt Hilda.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:56.420
"Everything has a price.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:57.890
That's how witchcraft works."

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:00.040
"But I don't think there's a price for me.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.040
Not anymore.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:04.600
I think I've tapped into a different kind
of magic.

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.880
One that isn't based on cause and effect.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.630
It feels different."

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:12.690
"You are racking up a cosmic debt the like
of which the world's never seen."

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:17.570
As Sabrina's friends later discover, her display
of extraordinary powers is actually a harbinger

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:19.210
of a dreadful future.

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:23.430
The mosaic they discover in the Greendale
mines shows that the Dark Lord plans for Sabrina

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:27.150
to be the Herald of Hell, in other words,
the bringer of the Apocalypse.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:32.030
After Lucifer arrives in Greendale, he orders
Sabrina to blow the horn of Gabriel and open

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:36.720
the gates of Hell so the VIPs of the underworld
can attend her coronation as their Queen.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:40.870
Lilith, who has served the Dark Lord all this
time in the belief that she would be the one

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:45.890
ascending to the throne, decides she's fed
up of being constantly cast aside by Lucifer.

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:50.870
We do see a slightly softer side to Madam
Satan when she meets Ms Wardwell's boyfriend

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:54.680
Adam and discovers the possibility of a loving
relationship.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:59.360
But when the Dark Lord finds out about Lilith's
secret relationship, he cruelly kills Adam

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:00.890
and serves him up on a platter.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:05.730
So by the time of the finale, when Lucifer
rejects Lilith again, she decides to team

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:09.720
up with Sabrina and the Spellmans to defeat
the Dark Lord.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:13.100
After a failed attempt to kill Lucifer in
the woods, they concoct a different scheme

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:17.739
to entrap him in the Acheron Configuration
that held the sleep demon Batibat.

00:04:17.739 --> 00:04:21.550
Sabrina and the coven put on a masquerade
dance and Sabrina then captures Lucifer in

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:26.240
Edward Spellman's Acheron, however, it doesn't
hold for long and the devil breaks out.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:30.480
When Lilith explains that the only prison
stronger than the Acheron is the human body,

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:34.030
Nick Scratch offers himself as a host body
to keep Lucifer imprisoned.

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:38.881
Nick, who's studied Edward's teachings, says
he's "the best binder and conjuror since Edward

00:04:38.881 --> 00:04:43.240
Spellman" and believes he's the only one strong
enough to contain the devil.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:47.360
And so Nick Scratch becomes the devil himself,
something that's always been hinted at in

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:51.080
his name as "Old Nick" and "Old Scratch" are
nicknames for the Devil.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:55.380
Nick's actions are also a way for him to redeem
himself for secretly betraying Sabrina to

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:56.400
the Dark Lord.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:00.480
By the way, a nice detail in this scene and
episode is the name of the dance that Sabrina

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:04.690
and Lucifer perform at the masquerade, The
Mephisto Waltz, which is also the name of

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:09.190
a 1971 horror movie about Satanists and body
swapping.

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:14.270
And after Lucifer is defeated, Lilith finally
gets the job she's been wanting forever: Queen

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:15.270
of Hell.

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:18.870
She takes Nick's body down with her to make
sure Lucifer doesn't escape.

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:21.970
Before she leaves, though, she restores Sabrina's
"witch abilities".

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:25.180
"So now, my dear, you have both power and
freedom.

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:28.400
And may you never give up either again."

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:32.200
It's unclear at this point if these include
the full powers we saw on display that came

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:36.540
from her infernal heritage or if it's just
regular witch powers.

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:41.520
CAOS Season 2 doesn't just overturn the established
order in the underworld.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:45.800
When Lucifer meets with Father Blackwood,
the Dark Lord mocks the new Church of Judas

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:48.560
that Blackwood has imposed on the Greendale
coven.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:53.800
In fact, Lucifer orders Blackwood to bow down
to Sabrina, telling him his church must report

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:54.870
to her.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:58.960
Blackwood is furious, as he knows Sabrina
is opposed to the misogynist and regressive

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:03.200
rules he's enforced in the church, plus he
also plotted to kill Sabrina and her family

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.110
including Ambrose.

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:09.680
Blackwood is so enraged that, rather than
hand power over the coven to Sabrina, he poisons

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.830
them all except his daughter Prudence and
his twins.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:17.240
Prudence is horrified by this and his plans
to continue the Blackwood line by marrying

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:21.650
his twins to each other and, with the help
of the Spellmans, they manage to save Agatha,

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:24.430
Dorcas and some of the other witches and warlocks.

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:29.100
We also discovered this season, as many of
us already suspected, that Blackwood was responsible

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:32.810
for engineering the plane crash that killed
Edward and Diana Spellman.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:37.260
The irony for Blackwood is that despite his
efforts to block Edward Spellman's reforms,

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:41.050
one of the tenets from Spellman's manifesto
has now become a reality; that "all witches

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:44.110
must be revered as the matriarchs of the Church
of Night."

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:49.480
So with Blackwood's departure, Zelda has now
become the Church's High Priestess.

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:53.620
Blackwood's future looks bleak, with a vengeful
Prudence and Ambrose ready to hunt him down

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:55.980
next season with swords and crossbows.

00:06:55.980 --> 00:07:00.120
Signalling that Blackwood's reign over their
Church is over, Prudence decapitates the Judas

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:05.260
statue he installed at the academy, possibly
also foreshadowing her father's eventual fate.

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:10.230
I also wonder whether there'll be any long-lasting
effects from the Ring a Ring o' Roses incantation

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:12.290
that the Weird Sisters were performing.

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:16.349
In modern times, the traditional rhyming song
has been associated with the plague and we

00:07:16.349 --> 00:07:20.290
did briefly see Blackwood's nose bleeding
while the sisters were singing it.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:24.430
Whether there'll be any lasting ill effects
on Blackwood though remains to be seen.

00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:28.590
With Sabrina clearer about her origins and
future now, she's much freer to spend more

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:33.001
time with her mortal friends Harvey, Roz and
Theo who were often off doing their own thing

00:07:33.001 --> 00:07:34.900
by themselves in Part 2.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:38.730
In fact, Sabrina recognises that the trio
managed to keep the demonic hordes at bay

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:43.550
by themselves when they held the gates of
Hell closed; so she realises she doesn't need

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:45.430
to protect them all the time.

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:49.470
Indeed, Sabrina suggests they team up for
what Harvey calls the Fright Club.

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:53.710
And Sabrina comes up with their first mission
which is to go to Hell and bring Nick back.

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:57.870
Now, that sounds like it could be fun, but
it seems pretty likely that something will

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:00.940
go wrong and Lucifer will end up escaping.

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:05.530
And although Lilith has gone to hell, thankfully
we'll still be seeing actress Michelle Gomez

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:09.800
on the show as the original Ms Wardwell is
back, so we'll be finding out if she suffered

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:13.480
any side effects from Lilith inhabiting her
body.

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:17.030
Sabrina also mentioned she's going to look
into her mother's side of the family.

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:21.180
That could be really interesting especially
if the other baby we saw at Sabrina's birth

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:25.280
isn't just symbolic of her dual nature but
is actually a secret twin!

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:28.600
Until we find out, I've got a theory video
on all the possibilities which you should

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:32.449
check out by tapping in the top right or click
the link in the video description.

00:08:32.449 --> 00:08:35.380
So, what did you think of Sabrina Season 2?

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:38.899
And do you have any theories or ideas on what
you'd like to see next season?

00:08:38.899 --> 00:08:40.689
Leave your thoughts in the comments below.

